Hey folks, I discovered a way to separate the glass from the gems.
When you throw a worthless piece of glass at a unicorn, the message
reads "the unicorn graciously accepts your gift." But when you throw
a real gem, it says "the unicorn gratefully accepts your gift."  So
when you're carrying around 5 blue gems and want to make sure they're
worthless before you dump 'em, throw 'em at a unicorn and see what's
what.  (also, throwing glass at a unicorn does nothing for your luck,
either way, in 3.1.  so this is a way to see if your luck's been 
helped by this tactic.).

If there are any other ways to ID gems without using scrolls of identify
(for us non-archaeologists), please do tell.

